<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese builder may have bought S.Costa - paper.</title>
<headline>Portuguese builder may have bought S.Costa - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese construction firm Teixeira Duarte is believed to have agreed with shareholders of another builder Soares da Costa to buy their stakes in the company, Semanario Economico newspaper reported.</p>
<p>The paper, which did not reveal its sources, said shareholders Fiat Impresit, which controls 25 percent, and businessman Salvador Caetano, who controls 20 percent, were unhappy with the performance of Soares da Costa shares.</p>
<p>Lisbon bourse interrupted trade in Soares da Costa shares after the newspaper report, a bourse spokesman said.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
